  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Suppose $A=P D P^{-1}$, where $P$ is a $3 \\times 3$ invertible matrix and $D=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]$. Let $B=2 I+3 A+A^{2}$, which of the following is true?",
    "solution": [
      1
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "ce942729-d79a-4a5f-89a1-cefea22bcbe7",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "$B$ is not diagonalizable.",
